WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
Speaker 1: Let's see who else&nbsp;
is on today. Why don't we speak&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:10.880
next to let's speak to Logan from&nbsp;
Eureka. Logan, you're on the air.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.760
Hey, can you hear me? Yes, I can.
Speaker 2: How are you doing? I'm doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:23.840
well. Cool. I just wanted to get your general take&nbsp;
on the upcoming California gubernatorial recall.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.480
A lot of the sentiment I get I am a&nbsp;
bartender personally, so I get a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:38.000
quips from my local community. And it seems like&nbsp;
in general, people don't know what they're talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.760
about. As far as why this is happening&nbsp;
and why do you think people hate Gavin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.880
Newsom so much is mostly what my question is.
Speaker 1: You know, to me, this recall effort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:58.240
makes no sense whatsoever. California is growing&nbsp;
almost as quickly over the last six, seven years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:04.320
as the developing country of China.&nbsp;
Economically, California is doing really well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.880
It whether whether you believe it's because&nbsp;
of Gavin Newsom or not, that's something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.360
that can be debated. But it seems to me that I&nbsp;
would be looking at Californians saying, wow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.040
on a lot of fronts, things are looking good.&nbsp;
They've got a surplus. They've got a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.760
interesting initiatives. Now, those on the right&nbsp;
like to say you've got homelessness in cities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.720
It's really expensive in California, et cetera.&nbsp;
You know, it's expensive because there's demand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:36.160
The very people who talk about markets&nbsp;
seem not to understand it's expensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.640
in California because a lot of people want to&nbsp;
go to California. That's why property values&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.880
are as high as they are. Is that bad for tons of&nbsp;
people? Of course it is. And we should deal with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.920
that. We should deal with a housing program.&nbsp;
We should deal with all these things. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:54.320
I am seeing nothing going on in California that&nbsp;
says to me the governor is uniquely failing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.120
needs to be removed before his term would&nbsp;
even be up. So you'd have to ask someone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.640
wants to do it because it makes no sense to me.
Speaker 2: Yes, that's pretty much where I'm at.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.080
But yeah. Thanks for responding.
Speaker 1: My pleasure. Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.655
we'll continue to follow that and see what&nbsp;
happens. Let's go next to. Oh, how about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.655 --> 00:02:16.694
Veronica? Veronica, what's on your mind today?
Speaker 2: Vello. Veronica. Oh, no, Sam Ceder.&nbsp;

00:02:16.694 --> 00:02:19.229
Speaker 1: All right, no,&nbsp;
Veronica, today, that's too bad.

